  "worked_solution": "By the multiplication law for conditional probability, the required conditional probability is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le Y\\le 3\\,|\\,X=1) & =\\frac{P((1\\le Y\\le 3),X=1)}{P(X=1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=1,(1\\le Y\\le 3))}{P(X=1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(X=1,Y=1)+P(X=1,Y=2)+P(X=1,Y=3)}{P(X=1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(1,3)}{{f}_{X}(1)},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(1) & =f(1,0)+f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(1,3) \\\\  & =0.1+0+0.3+0.05 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, we have that $f(1,1)=0,f(1,2)=0.3$ and $f(1,3)=0.05.$ \n\nFinally, substituting our values into our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le Y\\le 3\\,|\\,X=1) & =\\frac{f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(1,3)}{{f}_{X}(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+0.3+0.05}{0.45} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.35}{0.45} \\\\  & \u22480.78.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
